    <!-- Help guide sheet -->
    <string name="help_title">Kuroko Teleport Guide &amp; Parameter Reference</string>
    <string name="help_subtitle">System-side per-UID simulation · Zero target app injection</string>

    <string name="help_sec1_title">1. Quick Start in 3 Steps</string>
    <string name="help_sec1_b1_head">Step 1 · Select Target Apps</string>
    <string name="help_sec1_b1_body">Tap \"Target Apps\" and select apps to simulate (isolated per UID globally; switching routes or saved points does not alter your selected apps).</string>
    <string name="help_sec1_b2_head">Step 2 · Pick Mode &amp; Place Points</string>
    <string name="help_sec1_b2_body">Switch between \"Static\" and \"Motion\" in the bottom panel. Pan the map to align the center crosshair, then pick a point or tap \"+ Point\". Drag the panel handle up or down to smoothly expand or collapse.</string>
    <string name="help_sec1_b3_head">Step 3 · Start Simulation</string>
    <string name="help_sec1_b3_body">Tap the green \"Start Hold\" or \"Start Motion\" button to activate immediately. Collapsing the bottom panel opens %1$d%%+ unobstructed map view while quick buttons track along smoothly.</string>

    <string name="help_sec2_title">2. Profiles, Auto-Save Draft &amp; Long-Press Presets</string>
    <string name="help_sec2_b1_head">Auto-Restore Workspace (No Lost Drafts)</string>
    <string name="help_sec2_b1_body">Your active route draft, static pin, separate static/motion GPS jitter, pace, variation, carry posture, and map camera are automatically saved and restored on relaunch.</string>
    <string name="help_sec2_b2_head">Route Profiles (Full Profile / Path Only)</string>
    <string name="help_sec2_b2_body">Saving a route bundles its waypoints, lap limit, speed, pace variation, posture, and jitter. Tap a card to load the full profile, or tap \"Path Only\" to swap only the track while keeping your current pace. Active profiles support Update, Save as New, and one-tap clipboard JSON export/import.</string>
    <string name="help_sec2_b3_head">Custom Speed Presets (Long-Press to Save)</string>
    <string name="help_sec2_b3_body">After tuning your preferred speed, pace variation, and posture in Motion mode, long-press any preset chip (Walk / Jog / Run / Sprint) to overwrite it. Restore defaults anytime in Settings.</string>

    <string name="help_sec3_title">3. Key Parameters Explained</string>
    <string name="help_sec3_b1_head">Hand Swing vs Pocket</string>
    <string name="help_sec3_b1_body">Controls synthesized phone pitch and swing amplitude. \"Hand Swing\" models holding the screen tilted ~30° upward with wider arm swing; \"Pocket\" models an ~80° upright phone in a pocket or waist pack with tighter rotation so accelerometer and gyroscope waveforms match real carry habits.</string>
    <string name="help_sec3_b2_head">Pace Variation (%1$d%%–%2$d%% recommended)</string>
    <string name="help_sec3_b2_body">Real runners never move at a robotic constant speed. Setting ±%1$d%% introduces dual-timescale natural pace drift plus slight corner slowdowns, with the live fastest–slowest pace range shown on the panel.</string>
    <string name="help_sec3_b3_head">GPS Jitter (Default 2.0m)</string>
    <string name="help_sec3_b3_body">Simulates colored slow drift of real outdoor GNSS signals so recorded tracks avoid unnatural ruler-straight lines.</string>
    <string name="help_sec3_b4_head">RF Isolation &amp; Spoof Policies</string>
    <string name="help_sec3_b4_body">\"Full Spoof\" synthesizes geo-matched Cell towers, regional Wi-Fi AP lists, and BLE beacons; \"Strict Hide\" conceals real Wi-Fi, cell towers, and BLE; \"Outdoor\" hides indoor Wi-Fi while preserving real local cell towers. Expand any app card for per-radio Pass/Hide/Spoof control.</string>

    <string name="help_sec4_title">4. Top Hardware Status LED Legend</string>
    <string name="help_led_engine_tag">ENG ●</string>
    <string name="help_led_engine_desc">kuroko_daemon background service is connected via local auth (127.0.0.1:28765)</string>
    <string name="help_led_loc_desc">system_server shared-memory link ready (Location / GNSS / NMEA / Wi-Fi active)</string>
    <string name="help_led_phone_desc">com.android.phone link ready (Strict cell-tower hiding active)</string>
    <string name="help_led_sensor_desc">Native pedometer &amp; 5-axis IMU sensor hook ready (steps / cadence / accel / gyro / orientation; if S× appears, check KSU module v%1$s and Zygisk Next)</string>

    <string name="help_sec5_title">5. Safe Finishing &amp; LSPosed Scope Rules</string>
    <string name="help_sec5_b1_head">Auto-Hold on Completion (No Instant Teleport)</string>
    <string name="help_sec5_b1_body">When your target laps or distance is reached, the engine switches to \"Done · Holding\" at the finish point instead of shutting off abruptly. Switch back to your fitness app, finish and upload the workout first, then return to Kuroko Teleport and tap \"Stop\".</string>
    <string name="help_sec5_b2_head">LSPosed Scope Rule</string>
    <string name="help_sec5_b2_body">In LSPosed Manager, enable ONLY \"System Framework (android)\", \"Phone Services (com.android.phone)\", and optionally \"Bluetooth (com.android.bluetooth)\" for BLE hooks. Never enable any target app! All per-UID isolation happens seamlessly at the system layer.</string>

    <string name="help_sec6_title">6. Floating HUD &amp; Notification Controls</string>
    <string name="help_sec6_b1_head">Smart Auto-Hide (Appears in Background)</string>
    <string name="help_sec6_b1_body">Tap the HUD icon in the top bar or enable \"Floating HUD\" in Settings and grant \"Display over other apps\". With \"Auto-Hide Inside Kuroko Teleport\" enabled by default, the capsule appears automatically when switching to target apps and hides when returning to Kuroko Teleport so the map stays unobstructed.</string>
    <string name="help_sec6_b2_head">Edge-Docked Capsule &amp; Drag-to-Close</string>
    <string name="help_sec6_b2_body">The capsule displays a 6dp status LED with core distance/pace metrics and softly dims after 4 seconds of inactivity. Release to snap to the left/right screen edge, or drag into the bottom-center \"× Drag here to close\" hotzone to dismiss.</string>
    <string name="help_sec6_b3_head">Expanded Mini Console (252dp Quick Controls)</string>
    <string name="help_sec6_b3_body">Tap the capsule to expand the mini console in place: pause/resume/stop, nudge speed by ±0.3 m/s, apply any of the 4 speed presets, toggle Hand/Pocket posture, or reset steps with two-tap confirmation. Drag the top bar to reposition freely.</string>
    <string name="help_sec6_b4_head">Notification Controls &amp; Screen-Capture Stealth</string>
    <string name="help_sec6_b4_body">While active, a low-priority notification offers quick Pause / Resume / Stop / Close HUD buttons. Enable \"Hide from Screenshots/Recording (FLAG_SECURE)\" in Settings anytime. Set Kuroko Teleport battery optimization to \"Unrestricted\" in system battery settings to prevent background termination.</string>

